    "name": "Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port to Roncesvalles",
    "theme": "Initiation",
    "narrative": "The Pyrenees crossing is the hardest day and it is the first day. This is not an accident. The route breaks you open before you have built up defenses. The climb strips away everything you thought you needed — the extra weight in your pack, the pace you imagined you'd keep, the version of yourself you planned to be. Many pilgrims arrive in Roncesvalles having cried for reasons they cannot articulate.",
    "closing": "What did you carry up that mountain that you did not need?",
